  "explanations": {
    "initialized-nameplate": "Old five-argument MotorPowerFactor constructor left frequency/RPM/class/specified efficiency uninitialized. Complete nameplate input makes the near-zero branch deterministic. User separately approved this correction after reviewing before/after values.",
    "current-normalization-rounding": "Required percentage-to-fraction normalization changes the selected reference-current scale. Supplied-FLA normalization cancels that scale mathematically, but floating-point multiplication/division leaves a last-bit difference. Reproducing the old percent input with the new function reproduces the captured old value; displayed currents are identical.",
    "motor-performance-percentage": "The form supplies 90 percent but the retained MotorPerformance wrapper passed 90 as a fraction, yielding efficiencies near 9000 percent. Passing 0.90 corrects efficiency and power factor. The specified zero-load path also receives initialized Suite nameplate fields; the zero sign changes without a displayed efficiency change. Approved during planning."
  },
